  "scope": "0.10.1-claudegpt.28: no 'done' while background work runs. At Stop, claude's direct children named bash/sh/pwsh/powershell/cmd.exe at least 5 s old (and not older than claude) count as tool shells; with any, the session is idle with background work (status 'background' in reframe, 'Idle, background work running' / 'Bereit, Hintergrundarbeit läuft', busy colour dimmed) and no done is announced. Only those sessions are rechecked every 20 s; with none left it becomes idle and announces done. A new turn, registry busy/waiting or a Notification ends the wait; WSL is not checked. Same rule in the Rust host (reframe-conpty toolhelp child listing, reframe-sessions), the Node host (koffi toolhelp in src/main/win32.ts, src/ptyhost/sessions.ts) and SessionManager. sessions service version 2: status events carry background: true with status idle (older clients see idle); no protocol bump. Unit tests for the rule in Rust and TypeScript; a conformance scenario with a fake claude spawning a long-lived cmd.exe, run on both hosts against SessionManager.",
